  "slug": "environmental-microbiomes-e3ba",
  "summary": "Long-read and T2T assemblies now resolve structural variation at lineage scale, enabling trait association directly on SVs in graph pangenomes.",
  "synthesis": "Across these three studies, long-read, gap-free or chromosome-scale assemblies serve as the substrate for variation-aware comparison across crop and grass lineages. The longan study pairs a T2T gap-free genome and graph pangenome from 101 accessions with SV calling, selective sweep detection, and SV-GWAS that links structural variation to a DlDAZ-proximal region. The grain amaranth pangenome catalogs over 100,000 structural variants and reports domestication-associated changes in SV diversity and function alongside flowering-time QTL. The diploid Bromus assemblies, with contig N50 up to 294.76 Mb, characterize centromeric and sub-telomeric satellite repeats. What is new is trait association performed directly on structural variation within graph representations of lineage-level variation, while the Bromus work contributes assembly-level resolution of repeat architecture.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-10"
}
